"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.653664,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0219953,"nucleus_score":0.575136,"pct_ad":0.297679,"pct_control":0.293664,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.951687,"donor_log2fc":0.0225016,"donor_lfcse":0.0718254,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00673295},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"FAF2","gene_symbol_current":"FAF2","gene_id":"ENSG00000113194","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.187329,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0807895,"nucleus_score":-1.71183,"pct_ad":0.347152,"pct_control":0.35851,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.0341095,"donor_lfcse":0.0753272,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-6.15683e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"FAF2","gene_symbol_current":"FAF2","gene_id":"ENSG00000113194","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.275667,"nucleus_log2fc":0.036484,"nucleus_score":1.19263,"pct_ad":0.288223,"pct_control":0.28518,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.954198,"donor_log2fc":0.0266809,"donor_lfcse":0.0666727,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0052194}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000113194","module":"blue","kme":0.00605861,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.506562,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000113194","module":"blue","kme":0.106747,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000113194","entrez_id":["23197"],"uniprot":["Q96CS3"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is highly expressed in peripheral blood of patients with atopic dermatitis (AD), compared to normal individuals. It may play a role in regulating the resistance to apoptosis that is observed in T cells and eosinophils of AD patients. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q96CS3","text":"Plays an important role in endoplasmic reticulum-associated degradation (ERAD) that mediates ubiquitin-dependent degradation of misfolded endoplasmic reticulum proteins (PubMed:18711132, PubMed:24215460). By controlling the steady-state expression of the IGF1R receptor, indirectly regulates the insulin-like growth factor receptor signaling pathway (PubMed:26692333). Recruits ATPase VCP to lipid droplets and also binds to phospholipase PNPLA2/ATGL, inhibiting PNPLA2 activity by promoting its dissociation from its ABHD5/CGI-58 activator (PubMed:23297223). This inhibits PNPLA2-mediated triacylglycerol hydrolysis and leads to inhibition of lipid droplet degradation (PubMed:23297223). Involved in stress granule disassembly: associates with ubiquitinated G3BP1 in response to heat shock, thereby promoting interaction between ubiquitinated G3BP1 and VCP, followed by G3BP1 extraction from stress granules and stress granule disassembly (PubMed:34739333)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}